course: dictionary
lesson: 1549
title: One word, many rooms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Look at what is around the word. «A cow's stomach has four chambers, an alpaca's three.» You can count chambers in a stomach, so a chamber here is a closed space inside a body part, not a room with a door.
explain: «An apple cut across shows a star of five seed chambers, each with up to two seeds.» The seeds sit inside the apple, so each chamber is a small, closed space inside something bigger. Now try your meaning in the sentence: does «a small closed space inside» still make sense? It does, so you have it right.
explain: Now compare «the king's chamber» in an old story. Here the word means a private room, like a bedroom. «The upper chamber of parliament voted on the new law» is different again: here a chamber is a group of lawmakers. Same word, three meanings, and only the clues tell you which one to choose.
fact: A chamber is a room, or a closed space inside something.
fact: The heart has four chambers, and a cow's stomach has four chambers too.
fact: A council chamber is a large room used for meetings, and «the king's chamber» was a private room.
fact: A chamber can also be a group of lawmakers, such as one house of a parliament.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
exercise: «A cow's stomach has four chambers, an alpaca's three.» What does chamber mean here? | *A closed space inside a body part | A large room for a council meeting | A kind of farm animal | A tall tower on a castle
exercise: «The upper chamber of parliament voted on the new law.» What is a chamber in this sentence? | A bedroom | *A group of lawmakers, such as one house of parliament | A tall tower | A cave under a hill
exercise: «The king's chamber was at the top of the castle.» What does chamber mean here? | *A private room, like a bedroom | A type of bird | A loud noise | A place where sea creatures live
test: «Mudskippers keep water in their gill chambers.» What are gill chambers? | Holes dug by crabs | Small ponds in the mud | Fins that help the fish swim | *Closed spaces inside the fish's body
test: «The council chamber was full of people waiting for the vote.» What is a chamber here? | A bed for sleeping | *A large room used for a special purpose | A small cave in the rocks | A cupboard for coats
exam: «The lub-dub sound is the heart's valves snapping shut: «lub» when the valves between the upper and lower chambers close.» Where are the valves for the lub sound? | *Between the upper and lower chambers | In the stomach | On the outside of the skin | At the exits of the heart
